From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:21:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 005/207] deepseek: fail fast when CUDA context health is lost
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Own a host monitor from TP startup through model teardown so a sticky context fault reaches the existing fail-fast channel without waiting for an HTTP health poll. Readiness and admission already observe the published context fault before notification.

Host regressions cover each rank, once-only notification, independent thread detection and joined shutdown. This addresses justonehe’s issue #31 recovery report and ilonalumina’s additional rank-specific incidents; the original kernel fault remains unqualified.
